          "jcr:created": "Thu Sep 10 2020 13:09:36 GMT+0000",
          "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
          "text": "<h2><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\"><span style=\"color: #4c7d7a;\"><span style=\"color: #000000;\"><span style=\"color: #ffb500;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-75em\">Smart emergency communication that goes beyond a panic button</span></span></span></span></span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">Effective school safety starts with fast, clear communication. But traditional panic alarms can only go so far. That’s why it’s important to consider adopting mobile, two-way communication tools that help staff respond quickly and stay connected.</span></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"urw-egyptienne\">This white paper explores seven best practices for school emergency communication—from portable panic devices with geo-location to tools that support both crisis response and day-to-day campus operations.</span></span></p>\n",
